{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994246889046001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"fizz-god-dip","assignee":"","author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":6},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"Fix pushed to Gerrit as change 286 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/286). Adds undocumented --include-provenance flag to `show`; default view now strips managed_refs, reconciler (_read_local_ticket_full) always passes the flag. Local: lint+mypy+34 affected tests green; verified end-to-end on kooky-graft-cap. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified votes.","timestamp":1783226499197280001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"Patchset 1 CI caught a real regression: test_llm_parity_show_vs_list — to_llm actually passes managed_refs through (not in OMIT_KEYS), so stripping before the llm branch broke show<->list llm parity. Fixed by scoping the strip to the default (non-llm) view only (guard 'fmt != llm'); the reconciler uses the default format + --include-provenance, and the llm view is left intact for parity. Local: lint+mypy green, 897 passed in affected suites incl. the parity test. Patchset 2 pushed; re-awaiting votes.","timestamp":1783228012591385001}],"created_at":1783225488601572001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Summary\n`rebar show` (and its JSON output) surfaces the internal `managed_refs` provenance\nprojection in a way that reads as a **live `relates_to` link**, even after that link\nhas been removed with `unlink`. This makes a correctly-removed link look like it is\nstill present, and makes `unlink` look broken when it is working correctly.\n\n## Context / root cause\n`managed_refs` (`src/rebar/reducer/_managed_refs.py`) is a **strictly-monotonic**\nprojection of every logical reference a ticket has *ever* managed. Per its own module\ndocstring (lines 32-38) and `add_managed_ref` (\"Never removes\", lines 92-103) it is\n**deliberately never pruned by UNLINK/detach** — it exists so a local link/parent\nremoval can be propagated to a peer system (Jira) without being resurrected by the\nnext inbound sync. That behavior is correct and intentional for reconciliation.\n\nThe problem is purely **presentation**: `show` renders `managed_refs` alongside the\nlive link data with a `relates_to <target>` shape indistinguishable from an active\nrelation, with nothing marking it as \"removed / provenance-only.\" The live link set\n(`deps`) is the source of truth for what links actually exist.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n1. `rebar link A B relates_to`  (creates the link).\n2. `rebar unlink A B`  (removes it; reciprocal side removed too for relates_to).\n3. `rebar deps A`  → shows `deps: []` (link is genuinely gone).\n4. `rebar show A`  → still shows `managed_refs: [[\"relates_to\", \"B\"]]`.\n5. `rebar unlink A B` again → `Error: no LINK event found …` (confirms nothing to remove).\n\n- **Expected:** after unlink, `show` does not present B as a current `relates_to`\n  relation of A. Any provenance/ever-managed info is either hidden from the default\n  human view or clearly labeled as removed/provenance-only, distinct from live links.\n- **Actual:** `show` presents `managed_refs` such that B looks like a current\n  `relates_to` link of A, contradicting `deps: []` and misleading the reader into\n  thinking `unlink` failed.\n\n## Impact\n- Users (and agents) reading `show` conclude an unlinked relation is still present,\n  and that `unlink` is broken — wasted debugging (this bug was filed after exactly\n  that confusion). It undermines trust in the unlink/link surface.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a successful `unlink`, the default human `rebar show` output does not\n      present the removed relation as a current/live link.\n- [ ] If provenance (`managed_refs`) is shown at all in user-facing output, it is\n      clearly labeled as provenance/ever-managed (removed links distinguishable from\n      active ones) — not rendered identically to live `deps` relations.\n- [ ] The live link source of truth (`deps`) and the monotonic `managed_refs`\n      projection are visually/structurally distinct in `show`/JSON so they can't be\n      conflated.\n- [ ] `managed_refs` remains monotonic (this bug must NOT be \"fixed\" by pruning it on\n      UNLINK — that would reopen the Jira removal-resurrection window the field guards).\n- [ ] A regression test asserts that `show` for a ticket with a removed relates_to\n      link does not present it as an active relation.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0c4db0c6-f7f5-430a-b4e6-583ab6f35593","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b2e2-c631-3b0e-425c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar show surfaces monotonic managed_refs as a live link, making removed (unlinked) relations look present","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7d17af96-1bd8-4a9f-960c-e1814782535d","0c4db0c6-f7f5-430a-b4e6-583ab6f35593","48616a56-7cd6-4759-91ba-fe30a35da42a","0da006c4-1441-4c68-8a93-e2616309546d","e0fe0fcf-8c40-4a4b-a8e5-6adab18867b6","7ee39991-bdab-4fa5-8603-3d12112313bf"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994246889046001,"uuid":"3ce2e988-4736-4c7e-8d7b-c974af11d42f"}